@startuml
title Astral Project — Implemented Remote SFTP Session Path
skinparam shadowing false

participant "Local session client\n(target integration pending)" as LC
participant "OpenSSH / sshd" as SSH
participant "aspr-server\n(enrolled user)" as RS
participant "Broker bridge" as BB
participant "systemd-activated\nroot broker" as RB
participant "Safe resolver" as SR
participant "Native mount worker" as NW
participant "AppArmor-confined\nsftp-server" as SF
database "Granted objects" as FS

LC -> SSH : exact command aspr-channel-v1
SSH -> RS : restricted key starts forced entry
LC -> RS : uint32 length + canonical CBOR\nRemoteSessionRequestV1

group Enrolled-user validation before privileged dispatch
  RS -> RS : require exact command and transport key
  RS -> RS : decode exact fields; verify grant signature,\nhost ID, host-key fingerprint, user, and time
end

RS -> BB : open broker SFTP stream
BB -> BB : create AF_UNIX socketpair
BB -> RB : CreateNamespaceV1 + one stream FD\nvia SCM_RIGHTS

group Root broker authority gate
  RB -> RB : authenticate peer UID/GID with SO_PEERCRED
  RB -> RB : reverify signed grant and server identity
  RB -> RB : require every export within the per-root ceiling
  RB -> SR : resolve beneath configured trusted roots
  SR -> SR : open descriptor-relative; verify signed\ndevice, inode, mount ID, filesystem type, and kind
end

SR --> RB : ordered pinned source descriptors
RB -> RB : create and seal ExecutionPlanV1 memfd
RB -> RB : verify content-addressed runtime closure
RB -> NW : fixed FD launch: synchronization, plan,\nstream, log, sources, and runtime only
NW -> NW : unshare user + mount namespaces
RB <-> NW : install UID/GID maps; continue
NW -> NW : private mounts; tmpfs staging root
NW -> NW : open_tree + mount_setattr + move_mount
NW -> NW : attach runtime; pivot_root; drop capabilities
NW -> SF : fixed AppArmor transition and execve
RB --> BB : NamespaceReadyV1
BB --> RS : connected byte stream
RS --> LC : RemoteSessionReadyV1; raw SFTP follows

loop Until EOF, expiry, or worker failure
  LC -> SF : SFTP request through SSH and bridge
  SF -> FS : kernel-enforced granted operation
  FS --> SF : data/status
  SF --> LC : SFTP response through bridge and SSH
end

RB -> NW : terminate and reap on expiry

note over LC,RS
The rclone/aspr-transport producer of the local SFTP stream
belongs to the target architecture and is not yet integrated.
end note
@enduml
